; Stage 15 W8 (fn-pointer globals): `name-existing-kind` no longer calls a
; TY-FN-typed global "a function" on the strength of its type alone — it also
; asks `is-local`, which `emit-defvar` (and G-0's `prescan-defvar-name`) set to
; 1 while every function-registering path sets it to 0.
;
; The risk in that second conjunct is that it silences a GENUINE cross-kind
; collision. It must not: a real `defn` and a same-named function-pointer
; `defvar` are still two kinds of thing under one symbol, and one of them would
; emit `@f = global ptr null` alongside `define i32 @f(i32)`. The plain
; (non-fn-typed) collision is pinned by g0-value-fn-collision-order1/2; this is
; the fn-typed shape, the one the fix touches.

(defn f (x:i32):i32 (return x))

(defvar f:(fn i32)(i32) null)

(defn main ():i32
  (return (f 0)))
